  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "Spain, the reigning champions, led 1–0 through Xabi Alonso's penalty just before half-time in a rematch of the 2010 final. Louis van Gaal's Netherlands played with a back three and looked to go direct in behind."
    },
    {
      "label": "Build-up",
      "text": "Blind, with time on the left, looked up and hit a long diagonal over the Spanish midfield. Van Persie had already set off, running across the last defender as the ball was struck."
    },
    {
      "label": "Key moment",
      "text": "Casillas had come off the line to cover the space behind the defence. That left the goal exposed to anything lifted over the keeper rather than driven past."
    },
    {
      "label": "The finish",
      "text": "Instead of waiting for the ball to drop, van Persie dived full length and met it with the forehead, looping it up and over Casillas. The header needed height, not power, and dropped into the net."
    }
  ],
  "note": "Reconstructed from memory of the footage: Blind's long diagonal from the left and van Persie's diving header over Casillas are as they happened, but the passes before Blind, the Spanish defenders' positions, the exact spot of the header and kit details (Netherlands in their dark blue away kit, both goalkeeper shirts) are approximate. Commentary is original, not the broadcast."
}
